Vesper: refuse a request that changes an object bound read-only, or anything under it,
whatever name reaches it: another letter case, a hard link, a symbolic link, a moved directory.
The server reads the objects from <exports file>.protect and knows them by device and inode
number, not by a mount on one name (TD-073). The list is a file that the supervisor adds to
while the server runs: an object is in it before it is put at a protected place, and the
server reads what was added before it judges a request (TD-078). A directory on the way to a
read-only export inside a read-write one, an anchor, cannot be renamed or removed, so that a
client cannot change what the read-only export's path names (TD-080). The comment above
PROT_FIXED in Config/exports.y is the definition of the list.

